      "description": "Main festival celebration in New Glasgow, with live performances, local vendors, food demonstrations, kids’ activities, and a by-donation farm stand. Sunday performer timetable: Nico Romero Dada, 2:00–3:00pm; Filipino Dance Masters, 3:15–4:00pm; Wolf Castle, 4:00–4:35pm; Sweet Gale, 4:40–5:20pm; Fiver, 5:25–6:00pm. Listed activities include the Hot Pepper Challenge with the Burly Farmer; Natural Weaving with Rilla Marshall; Kids Craft Table with Becca the Witch; Stiltwalking with Laura Astwood; Fish Smoking with Chad Poirier; Bouquet Bar with Moss-bank Flower Farm; and Evelyn Bradley: Contemporary Food Practices of the African and Black Diaspora on PEI. A by-donation farm stand is also listed. The Sunday menu lists pastrami-crusted smoked pulled pork or Larkin’s chicken, plus a vegetarian cauliflower and squash gratin; dishes are served with Mediterranean barley salad and smashed potatoes, with glazed pumpkin cake for dessert. The listed acts, activities, vendors, and menu are included as part of the festival rather than separate events.",
